{% extends 'public/layout.html.twig' %}

{#
   A page belonging to this site, not a framework error screen.

   This is the single response for three different situations: an address that
   never existed, a draft, and something archived. They must be indistinguishable
   (FR-002, SC-002), so this template says nothing about which one happened —
   there is no "this article was withdrawn" branch, and there cannot be one,
   because the controllers throw the same exception without recording why.
#}

{% block title %}Not found — {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}

{#
   No preview metadata and no canonical address, and both halves of that matter.

   A 404 is not a page: there is nothing here to index, nothing to share and no
   canonical address to declare, so the tags feature 010 puts on every page are
   wrong here on their own terms.

   They also broke the rule this template exists for. `og:url` and the canonical
   link name the address that was asked for, so a 404 for a draft and a 404 for
   an address that never existed stopped being byte-for-byte identical. Nothing
   was disclosed — a reader is only shown the address they typed — but the
   identity is the property that is checked, and a proxy that has acquired
   exceptions stops protecting anything.
#}
{% block meta %}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
{% endblock %}

{% block main %}
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Not found</h1>

    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        There is nothing at this address.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm">
        <a href="{{ path('home') }}" class="text-accent no-underline hover:underline">&larr; Back to the front page</a>
    </p>
{% endblock %}
